  "analysis_guidance": [
    "Separate aggregate counts by their session, event, cart, or order grain. Independent counts alone do not prove an ordered funnel or step conversion.",
    "A step conversion requires a defined metric, common linked cohort, join keys, compatible time window, event ordering and deduplication. Do not divide order rows by checkout sessions and call the result conversion without this evidence.",
    "A descriptive ratio within a proven population can be reported with its numerator, denominator and scope. When cohort evidence is missing, present separate counts and the limitation; do not invent an event or claim.",
    "Within one analysis reuse successful schema and coverage observations for the same source, scope and observation time. Query again when freshness, changed inputs, failure or an explicit request requires it; never treat old quality as current."
